# KNOWN GAP (R41 T-FMT-B, 2026-08-11) — `gg fmt` DELETES the author's grouping
# parentheses.
#
# A redundant paren is not noise: it is how a reader is told which sub-expression
# to bind first. `(y % 4) == 0 and ((y % 100) != 0 or (y % 400) == 0)` says the
# arithmetic groups before the comparisons; the same line with every paren
# stripped means exactly the same thing to the compiler and something noticeably
# harder to a human. The formatter is not entitled to that edit.
#
# WRITE SITE: `parse_paren_expr`'s parenthesized-expression branch
# (`src/parser/expr.rs:1641-1645`) does `expect(RParen); Ok(first)` — the AST node
# IS the inner expression and the paren layer is gone, so nothing downstream can
# know it was written. The formatter re-emits only the parens ITS OWN precedence
# rules demand, which is why the outer `(… or …)` group below survives while
# every author paren inside it does not: that one is the formatter's, not the
# author's, and it is green for a reason unrelated to this gap.
#
# INTENDED (asserted by `fmt_preserves_author_parens`, `#[ignore]`d until the fix
# lands): every parenthesis below round-trips unchanged.
#
# OBSERVED at HEAD, all three cells:
#     (y % 4) == 0 and ((y % 100) != 0 …)  →  y % 4 == 0 and (y % 100 != 0 …)
#     n + (n * shift)                      →  n + n * shift
#     if (slen as bool):                   →  if slen as bool:
#
# The fix is a paren-emission CHOKEPOINT (Core #4), not a patch — the prototype
# that recorded author parens as parser trivia and deduped at
# `format_expr_maybe_parens` was NOT IDEMPOTENT, because
# `wrap_multiline_expr_in_parens` (`src/formatter/mod.rs:5168`) writes its
# broken-chain parens through `doc::if_break` unconditionally at the Doc layer,
# outside that dedup; pass 2 then reads the pair as an author paren and stacks
# another. Every unconditional paren write has to route through one dedup, with
# an arm-count guard so the next one cannot skip it. Full filing in `TODO.md`
# (Tooling / CLI / formatter / LSP).
#
# CELL AXIS: three costumes of ONE class — a redundant group around a
# higher-precedence binary operand, a redundant group around a whole arithmetic
# sub-term, and a redundant group around a cast in condition position. It does
# NOT sample the accretion shape (a chain long enough to break), which is the
# prototype's separate blocker and is described in the TODO entry.

bool is_leap(int y):
    return (y % 4) == 0 and ((y % 100) != 0 or (y % 400) == 0)

int scaled(int n, int shift):
    return n + (n * shift)

bool nonempty(int slen):
    if (slen as bool):
        return true
    return false

void main():
    print(f"{is_leap(2024)} {scaled(3, 4)} {nonempty(2)}")
